A note on what the attribution is for, since it matters more here than the
copyright does.

The value in this repository is not the Apex — each case is one line, and any
competent Salesforce developer could write all 28 in an afternoon. The value is
the `org_verdict` field: what a real Salesforce org actually did when that line
was executed as a user with known permissions, on Summer '26.

If you redistribute or build on this, keep the `label_provenance` field with
each case. It records whether a verdict was measured in an org, taken from
platform documentation, or merely reasoned — and a case separated from its
provenance is an assertion wearing the costume of a measurement. That
distinction is the only thing here worth protecting.
